<title>SINGAPORE: India tenders to sell Apr 25-27 Madras naphtha.</title>
<headline>India tenders to sell Apr 25-27 Madras naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has offered to sell by tender 28,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting April 25-27 from Madras on the east coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes on April 17 and bids will be valid for one day.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN tender from Madras, lifting March 27-29, was awarded at $22.28 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board (fob) basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3086)</p>
</text>
